Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 05/25/2023]
1. Er >= 495 keV: from Endt 1990. These are already normalized to Anderson et al. 1982, which we are also adopting as a standard at higher energies. 
2. Er = 375, 478, 484, 569 keV: Anderson et al. 1982.
3. Er = 419 keV: Powell et al. 1998.
4. Er = 305 keV: Dermigny et al. 2016.
5. Er = 245, 293 keV: Iliadis et al. 1990.
6. Er = 191 keV: Strieder et al. 2012, but the uncertainty on the strength has been increased.
7. Er = 93 keV: Strieder et al. 2012; Zhang et al. 2023, but the uncertainty on the strength has been increased to 50%.
8. Er = 38, 59, 109, 131 keV: partial widths estimated using transfer information presented in Iliadis et al. 1996. We assumed that Jp=4+ for Er = 38 keV,
   as guided by the shell model [see discussion in Iliadis et al. 1996].
9. Direct capture: experimental C2S values as tabulated in Endt 1990, but also including Li et al. 2020 for low-lying levels.
